Changelog: 14-11-2026 03:27:00

Breaking. Windows support is removed: the suite is for Bazzite. run.sh takes the Linux venv alone (it no longer
looks for a Windows venv under Git Bash). Nothing changes on Linux.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 00:36:00

Fixed. The emulator cards no longer fail with "HTTP Error 403: rate limit exceeded". GitHub was asked without a
sign-in, which allows 60 requests an hour for the whole address; the requests now carry the token of the machine's
gh login (or GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN), 5,000 an hour, and a token GitHub refuses is left out. When the limit is used
up the card says until when, and how to sign in. The tests no longer ask GitHub or gh.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 22:48:09

Fixed. Packages installed in a venv's lib64/ are found. On Fedora with Python 3.15 a venv's lib64/ is a folder of
its own, not a link to lib/, and pip puts packages with compiled parts there: PyQt6 and PyQt6-Charts were reported
missing in every app's venv while they were installed.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:54:16

Fixed. The catalog of the Bazzite Console Suite knows the suite's three new apps and what they need: System Overlay,
Fan Control and HDMI CEC Manager with their PyQt6, pkexec, systemctl and notify-send for Fan Control's thermal guard,
systemctl and cec-ctl (v4l-utils, which Fix can layer) for HDMI CEC Manager, and PyQt6-Charts for Bazzite Test, which
its requirements.txt names. An installed app the catalog did not list was not checked at all. New in the catalog too:
the FFmpeg inside Remote Play's native core. The check for it asked a module that is not this suite's
(bazzite_console_link_core); it asks ps5_remoteplay_core, the core Remote Play imports, in the app's own venv. The
tests are this suite's again: 31 of them still asked for the tools, apps and names of the suite the app came from
(stress-ng, setpci, flashrom, Decky Loader, Sony's firmware lists, "nexus-suite") and failed. They read this suite's
catalog now, and the checks it has no tool for (a tool that needs root, one of two commands, flashrom's internal
programmer, Homebrew before rpm-ostree, Decky and Sony's lists) run on entries the tests make themselves.

